          "Because the client wants to save money and the freelance editor wants higher direct pay, the agency owner is abruptly cut out of the relationship. The agency owner loses a loyal monthly retainer, suffers immediate revenue loss, and has effectively trained their own competitor using their own client relationships. Non-disclosure agreements (NDAs) and non-compete contracts offer virtually zero protection against this dynamic, particularly when hiring talented freelance editors across international borders where legal enforcement is practically impossible and financially unfeasible.",
          "The only foolproof solution to client poaching is architectural security: Two-Lane Masked Communication. Inside a purpose-built video editing agency management tool like Gigxomi, the client and the freelance editor operate in two completely isolated, parallel communication lanes. Lane 1 is the Client Relay: the client communicates exclusively with the agency brand through their preferred channel (such as WhatsApp Business or Instagram Direct). Lane 2 is the Production Relay: the freelance editor receives detailed assignment cards, timecoded creative briefs, raw footage download links, and revision checklists inside the workspace. The editor never sees the client’s real phone number, email address, or social handles. Client inquiries and editor submissions pass through the agency dashboard, preserving complete agency ownership of the client relationship forever.",
